  "worked_solution": "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202g}{\u2202y}=\\frac{\u2202g}{\u2202r}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{\u2202g}{\u2202\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202g}{\u2202r}=2r\\operatorname{cos}\u20613\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\u2202g}{\u2202\\theta }=-3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202g}{\u2202y} & =(2r\\operatorname{cos}\u20613\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta +\\frac{1}{r}(-3{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =r(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u20613\\theta -3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u20613\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
